Stage	Level	Core Focus Areas	What You Will Build
Module 1	Scratch: The Anatomy of an Agent	The ReAct (Reason + Act) loop, native tool calling, observation-action cycles, and building an agent in pure Python without frameworks.	A CLI-based autonomous research & calculator agent from scratch (~60 lines of Python).
Module 2	Beginner: Memory & Agentic RAG	Short-term (thread state) vs. long-term (episodic/semantic) memory. Upgrading passive RAG into Agentic RAG (query routing, self-grading retrieval, and query rewriting).	A technical documentation agent that verifies its own answers and re-queries when data is missing.
Module 3	Intermediate: Stateful Orchestration	Moving from brittle linear chains to cyclical graphs using LangGraph. State machines, conditional branching, error recovery loops, and Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) approval gates.	An automated triage & remediation agent that pauses execution to ask for human approval before running sensitive actions.
Module 4	Advanced: Multi-Agent & MCP	Multi-agent topologies (Supervisor vs. Swarm/Hierarchical), context isolation, handoffs using CrewAI / AutoGen / LangGraph, and the Model Context Protocol (MCP) for standardized tool integration.	A multi-agent software & security auditing crew (Planner, Code Analyzer, Sandboxed Executor, and Reporter).
Module 5	Pro: Production, Evals & Security	Tracing & observability (LangSmith/Arize), deterministic & LLM-as-a-Judge evaluation harnesses, cost/latency caching, sandboxed code execution, and defending against indirect prompt injection and excessive agency (OWASP Top 10 for LLMs).	A hardened, observable production agent pipeline with automated evaluation tests and strict security guardrails.
